            "title": "Australia August consumer sentiment boosted by rate cuts",
            "description": "",
            "summary": "SYDNEY (Reuters) -A measure of Australian consumer sentiment improved sharply in August as the third cut in interest rates this year bolstered the outlook for finances and the economy, a survey showed on Tuesday.  A Westpac-Melbourne Institute survey showed its main index of consumer sentiment climbed 5.7% in July to 98.5, the highest reading since early 2022.  The pick-up came after the Reserve Bank of Australia cut interest rates a quarter point to 3.60% and left the door open to further easing this year.",
